BANKWISE DEMO BANK
LOAN SERVICES GUIDE

1. INTRODUCTION

A loan is a financial service in which a lender provides funds to an eligible borrower. The borrower generally repays the borrowed amount according to agreed terms, which may include interest, fees, and scheduled repayments.

This is a fictional/demo document created for the BankWise AI RAG project. It is not an official banking policy.

2. TYPES OF LOANS

Banks may provide different types of loans, including:

• Personal loans
• Education loans
• Home loans
• Vehicle loans
• Business loans
• Other specialized loan products

The availability of loan products depends on the bank.

3. PERSONAL LOAN

A personal loan is generally an unsecured loan that may be used for eligible personal expenses.

Common factors considered by a lender may include:

• Income
• Employment status
• Credit history
• Existing financial obligations
• Repayment capacity
• Bank policies

Approval is not guaranteed.

4. EDUCATION LOAN

An education loan may help eligible students finance approved educational expenses.

Possible expenses may include:

• Tuition fees
• Examination fees
• Books
• Equipment
• Accommodation
• Other eligible education-related expenses

Eligibility and documentation vary between lenders and education programs.

5. HOME LOAN

A home loan is generally used for eligible housing-related purposes, such as purchasing or constructing a property.

Home loans may involve:

• Property-related documents
• Income verification
• Credit assessment
• Down payment requirements
• Repayment schedules

The exact requirements depend on the lender and loan product.

6. VEHICLE LOAN

A vehicle loan may be used to finance the purchase of an eligible vehicle.

The lender may consider:

• Applicant eligibility
• Income
• Credit history
• Vehicle information
• Repayment capacity

Loan terms and financing limits vary.

7. BUSINESS LOAN

Business loans may provide financing for eligible business activities.

A lender may request information such as:

• Business details
• Income or financial records
• Identity information
• Business documents
• Repayment information

Eligibility depends on the lender's policies.

8. LOAN ELIGIBILITY

Loan eligibility may depend on several factors.

These may include:

• Age
• Income
• Employment or business status
• Credit history
• Existing loans
• Repayment capacity
• Required documentation
• Bank-specific criteria

Meeting general eligibility conditions does not guarantee loan approval.

9. LOAN APPLICATION

A general loan application process may include:

Step 1: Select a suitable loan product.

Step 2: Review eligibility requirements.

Step 3: Submit the application through an official channel.

Step 4: Provide the requested documents.

Step 5: The lender evaluates the application.

Step 6: The lender communicates the decision according to its procedures.

10. DOCUMENTS FOR LOAN APPLICATION

Depending on the loan type, a lender may request:

• Identity proof
• Address information
• Income documents
• Employment information
• Bank statements
• Property or vehicle documents, where applicable
• Education-related documents, where applicable
• Other supporting documents

The exact documents vary by loan product and lender.

11. INTEREST RATE

An interest rate determines the cost of borrowing money.

Loan interest rates may vary based on:

• Loan type
• Borrower profile
• Credit history
• Loan amount
• Loan tenure
• Bank policy
• Market conditions

Customers should carefully review the applicable rate before accepting a loan.

12. LOAN TENURE

Loan tenure is the period over which the borrower repays the loan.

A longer tenure may reduce the amount of each scheduled payment but can increase the total interest paid over the life of the loan.

Customers should compare repayment options carefully.

13. EMI

EMI stands for Equated Monthly Instalment.

An EMI is a scheduled payment made by a borrower toward a loan.

An EMI generally consists of:

• Principal repayment
• Interest component

The amount depends on factors such as loan amount, interest rate, and tenure.

14. LOAN REPAYMENT

Borrowers should make scheduled repayments according to the agreed repayment schedule.

Missing repayments may result in:

• Additional charges
• Interest
• Negative impact on credit history
• Other consequences under the loan agreement

Customers should contact the lender if they experience repayment difficulties.

15. PREPAYMENT

Some loan products may allow borrowers to repay part or all of the outstanding loan before the scheduled end date.

Prepayment conditions and charges vary depending on the loan product and applicable terms.

Customers should check the loan agreement before making a prepayment.

16. LOAN PROCESSING FEES

Some lenders may charge processing or service fees when evaluating or providing a loan.

Customers should review all applicable charges before accepting a loan.

17. LOAN SECURITY

Some loans may be secured by an asset or other form of security, while others may be unsecured.

The security requirements depend on the type of loan and lender.

18. LOAN FRAUD AWARENESS

Customers should be cautious of fake loan offers.

Warning signs may include:

• Requests for confidential banking credentials
• Unexpected requests for OTPs or PINs
• Unofficial websites
• Pressure to pay unknown fees
• Guaranteed loan approval claims
• Requests to install unknown applications

Customers should verify loan offers through the lender's official website or branch.

19. BANKWISE AI LIMITATION

BankWise AI is an informational chatbot created for a demonstration RAG project.

It cannot:

• Approve loans
• Reject loans
• Calculate official eligibility
• Access credit records
• View bank accounts
• Process loan applications
• Disburse loan amounts
• Modify loan accounts

The chatbot provides general educational information only.

20. IMPORTANT INFORMATION

Customers should read the complete loan agreement before accepting a loan.

Important items to review include:

• Interest rate
• Loan amount
• Tenure
• EMI
• Processing fees
• Prepayment conditions
• Late payment charges
• Other applicable terms

DISCLAIMER

Loan products, eligibility criteria, interest rates, fees, documentation, repayment conditions, and approval procedures vary between banks and may change over time.

This document is for demonstration purposes only. Always verify current loan information through the relevant bank's official channels.
